 under the writable temporary root. Do not reuse a directory containing user data:
 pytest owns and may remove its selected base directory. Test counts and exact
 commands are retained in the Stage 2 evidence report.
+
+Gateway identifiers use the approved registration `text64` contract in every
+role: 1–64 ASCII characters, starting with a lowercase letter, followed by
+lowercase letters/digits with single dot, underscore or hyphen separators between
+nonempty components. They pass into REQUEST key 6 unchanged. They are not 32-byte
+operator/service IDs; no case folding, trimming, hashing or truncation is allowed.
+The example uses `gateway.fixture`. The previous numeric hex example was a
+configuration-to-registration defect; old evidence is retained. A cross-contract
+test inserts the example identifiers into the retained registration REQUEST and
+runs the actual approved body validator. This checks representation, not authority.
